==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈpɒl.stə(ɹ)/|/əˈpɐl.stə(ɹ)/|a=UK}}

===Etymology 1===
{{back-formation|en|upholsterer|t=tradesman who finishes furniture}},<ref>{{R:New English Dictionary|entry=Upho·lster|part of speech=v|volume=X|part=1|page=426|column=2|passage=Back-formation from {{smallcaps|Upholsterer}} or {{smallcaps|Upholstery}}.|nodot=1}}</ref> from {{inh|en|enm|upholdester}}, from {{der|en|enm|upholder|t=dealer in small goods}}, from {{m|enm|upholden|t=to repair, uphold}}; equivalent to {{af|en|uphold|-ster}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[fit]] [[padding]], [[stuffing]], [[spring]]s, [[webbing]] and [[fabric]] [[covering]] to ([[furniture]]).

